Author: rhyanz46 <<author-email>>
Date:   Thu Nov 19 15:51:39 2026 +0000

    perf(blocks): a block layout's pin set is judged by a local tally of the lines it changes, not the quality harness (b12a2c-squeeze fix round 4 #2, #3, #5)
    
    9a79456 let a block layout's static scene choose between a title side's
    pins dealt with its displaced entries as one set and the pins left where
    the ports stage put them by running the edge stages twice and calling
    `quality::measure` on both drawings. The harness is a yardstick, not a
    stage: wherever a side was dealt as a set it made `scene()` (and a cold
    `route()`, which is one static layout) up to ten times slower on the
    verifier's inputs (bench-75 with a five-pin frame added 48 -> 439 ms,
    dense-td with it 83 -> 578 ms; 91 of 1062 generated block-mode inputs
    more than 2x slower).
    
    - `edgepass::stages` runs the ports stage once and the ortho stage
      twice; the later stages run on both drawings only where the two ortho
      drawings differ (the set moved a pin), and the two are weighed by
      `Tally`: the edges the two drawings draw differently, measured against
      every other edge, node, chip and frame title near them (lines on one
      another, touching, a head beside another line, lines through a node or
      over a chip; crossings; a fan's crossings; lines past a frame title;
      entries through a frame's wall; ends on a node's flank; the smallest
      gap). Lines far from what changed are not sampled.
    - The tally counts a pin's head beside an entry as one line on another
      however near it is (#3): the set on the verifier's five-pin frame only
      moved such a pair from 0.4 to 1.6 px, past the harness's overlap
      counter, and was kept as a drawing that took an overlap away. It is no
      longer kept; that input draws as at the package start.
    - Chips are judged one by one (`labels::chip_off_line`, which replaces
      the summed `chips_off_lines`; #5): no chip of a changed edge farther
      off its own line than in the other drawing, within its own slack
      `CHIP_OFF_SLACK` (rounding) instead of the gap tolerance.
    
    Timing (suite-on, min of 5 per input): the verifier's bench-75 + five
    pins 428 -> about 70 ms against 30 ms at the package start (the second
    run of the later stages), dense-td + five pins 595 -> 105 against 82 ms;
    over the 1062 generated block-mode inputs the total is as at the start
    and 9 inputs are more than 2x slower (at most 2.8x, +2.4 ms), all where
    the set moves a pin. No repository fixture deals a side as a set: the
    three checks against the package start and against 1ae4222 say no worse
    on every cell, gate message and direction copy; the default build is
    byte-identical (25 corpus SVGs). Against 1ae4222 on the generated sets
    only the five-pin frame changes (back to its start drawing) and one
    drawing moves 1.3 px nearer at a 39 px gap.
    
    Tests: `a_pins_head_beside_an_entry_counts_as_one_line_on_another_however_near`,
    `a_chip_moving_off_its_line_is_not_paid_for_by_another_coming_back`.
    No snapshot or gate changed.
    
